    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the test passes. The audit output confirms correct behaviour: `registrationDate=2026-09-04` (September, \u2265 July) yields `membershipNumber=...-M26`, matching fiscal year FY26.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starting 1 July), keeping structural impact low by putting the logic in a small new cohesive utility so the edits to the large `OwnerMapper` class stayed minimal.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `util/FiscalYears.java`: three tiny, low-complexity static methods:\n- `startYear(date)` \u2014 calendar year the containing fiscal year began.\n- `label(date)` \u2014 `FY<YY>` string.\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years elapsed.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** (delegations only, no added complexity):\n- New `fiscalYear` DTO mapping + small `fiscalYear(owner)` helper returning `FY<YY>` from the (already business-day-adjusted) registration date.\n- `membershipNumber` year segment now uses the fiscal-year start year instead of the calendar year.\n- `tenureDays` (365-day counting) \u2192 `tenureFiscalYears` using `FiscalYears.elapsed`, and the membership-points rule now awards for tenure of at least one elapsed fiscal year.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**: added the read-only `fiscalYear` schema property (generates the DTO field/setter) and updated the `membershipNumber`/`membershipPoints` descriptions to match.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec didn't pin down the exact tenure-points threshold in fiscal-year terms, and no test covers it. I translated the old \"over 365 days\" (one year) to \"at least one elapsed fiscal year\" (`>= 1`). Easy to adjust to `> 1` if you intended strictly more than a full fiscal year.",
